**Design Approach:**
To implement a dual-edge triggered flip-flop that toggles on both clock edges, I'll use two separate flip-flops: one for the rising edge and one for the falling edge. Both flip-flops will capture the input `d` on their respective clock edges and drive the same output `q`. This approach simulates the dual-edge behavior by combining the outputs of two standard flip-flops.

**Implementation Details:**
- The rising-edge flip-flop captures `d` on the positive clock edge.
- The falling-edge flip-flop captures `d` on the negative clock edge.
- Both flip-flops drive the same output `q`, ensuring the output updates on both clock transitions.

[BEGIN]
module TopModule
(
  input  logic clk,
  input  logic d,
  output logic q
);

  // Rising-edge flip-flop
  always @(posedge clk) begin
    q <= d;
  end

  // Falling-edge flip-flop
  always @(negedge clk) begin
    q <= d;
  end

endmodule
